      "takeaway": "This survey systematically reviews the development of quadruped robots, covering joint configuration, dynamic locomotion control methods, and mobile manipulation approaches, with a focus on leg-arm collaborative robots and Whole-body Control (WBC) methods. It provides a structured comparison of gait switching, terrain adaptation, and disturbance resistance across different control paradigms, which is valuable for researchers seeking a broad landscape of quadruped design and control. For your work on legged robots and mobile manipulation, this survey serves as a reference to position your own contributions, identify underexplored gaps in leg-arm coordination or WBC, and inform design choices for new platforms or control frameworks.",
