      "title": "Sim-to-Real Learning for Humanoid Box Loco-Manipulation",
      "takeaway": "This paper presents a sim-to-real reinforcement learning approach for training box loco-manipulation skills on the bipedal humanoid robot Digit, addressing the challenge of whole-body coordination to lift and carry boxes of varying weight, position, and orientation while maintaining balance. The reward functions are designed to encourage desired box interactions while valuing balance and gait quality, and the learned skills are combined into a full system that successfully transfers to real hardware, marking the first demonstration of a learned controller for this task on a physical humanoid. For your research in legged robots and robot learning, this work offers a concrete example of designing reward structures for whole-body loco-manipulation and achieving sim-to-real transfer, which you can build upon by extending the approach to other manipulation tasks, different robot morphologies, or more complex environments.",
